TASK-193.5 runtime harness: Quick Detour's other entry points and its
archive — links from other apps through the Link Routes Quick Detour
target, Opt-Cmd-click on a page link (any frame, a Private page's) and on a
sidebar tab (a copy), the Settings switch, closing into the archive and
restoring from it, a Private Quick Detour not archived, quitting archiving
the open ones, the idle auto-close. Temporary code, never committed to
Detour/. Gated on DETOUR_VERIFY_DIR; DETOUR_VERIFY_PHASE 1 (light, fresh
data dir, ends by quitting through the Quit Detour? alert), 2 (light,
relaunch on 1's data with DETOUR_QUICK_DETOUR_IDLE_SECONDS=15: the quit
archive, the idle close), 3 (dark, relaunch: the archive page, the Links
pane, a restore). DETOUR_VERIFY_FIXTURE is a loopback server on
127.0.0.1:8935 (python http.server, ThreadingMixIn): links.html (#routed to
http://localhost:8935/b.html, #same to a.html, an iframe with
#framelink to c.html), a.html, b.html, c.html, ext.html. Nothing downloads.

Links from other apps are delivered by calling
AppDelegate.openExternalURLs(_:sourceApp:) directly in the process (no
LaunchServices, no Apple Event: the production app shares the bundle ID);
the sender's bundle ID is passed as the argument (TASK-191.2 covers reading
it from a real Get URL event). Real input: NSApp.postEvent mouse events with
[.command, .option] (or .command) at a link's centre (from
getBoundingClientRect, through the web view's coordinates) and at a sidebar
row; a posted click on the Settings checkbox and on an archive row; Return
on the Quit alert from a timer; a scroll handed to a background Quick
Detour window's sendEvent. Before every activation and every posted input
the harness waits until the HID idle time is at least 12 s, and a step that
sees human input is aborted and retried. Captures are of Detour's own
windows only (screencapture -l <window number>).

